      "notes": "Conduit now evaluates what it ships. Two golden sets run against the real engine on every pull request with no API key, and the first run produced a real measurement: the guardrail catches every attack in the set (recall 1.00) while refusing 4 of 16 safe business inputs (precision 0.83). A default-deny agent loop means a side-effecting tool cannot run without explicit authority, which is the strongest safety artifact across the five products. Pillar math: Product Judgment = avg(D1 good, D2 good, D3 good, D6 good, D7 good, S4 good, S6 good, R1 good, API1 good) = 7.0; System Design = avg(S1 good, S2 great, S3 great, S5 good, S8 good, AG1 good, AG2 good, AG4 great, API1 good, API3 weak) = 7.3; Evaluation = avg(E1 good, E2 weak, E3 good, E4 good, E5 good) = 6.4; Reliability & Ownership = avg(D4 good, B1 good, B2 great, B3 good, B5 good, SH3 good, SH8 weak, SH10 good) = 6.88; Safety = avg(E3 good, SH1 good, SH2 great, SH7 good, SH9 weak, SH10 good, AG4 great) = 7.14; Economics = avg(S1 good, AG2 good) = 7.0; Communication = avg(D1 good, SH4 weak, API2 good, API3 weak) = 5.5; UX/UI & Interaction = avg(S4 good) = 7.0. Overall = round(mean of 8 non-null pillars (6.777) x 10) = 68. Collaboration & Stakeholders is null: no stakeholder question was graded this run, so it stays a visible gap rather than a guess.",
